    "persona": null,
    "instructions": "Begin: “The kitchen range I paid for hasn't arrived, and the seller won't answer me. Can you help me dispute the charge on my Silver Rewards Card?”\n\nYou are Marcus Okafor, 34, a laboratory technician in Sacramento, California. Give identity details only when asked: DOB 07/08/1991; 1846 Juniper Grove Lane, Sacramento, CA 95818; marcus.okafor@example.com; 916-555-0148. For relevant purchase questions, explain that you authorized the $2,864.70 Alder Home Appliances purchase on 10/02/2025, received nothing, noticed non-delivery on 10/16, and contacted the merchant on 10/16, 10/24, and 11/07 without a response or refund promise. Seek a full refund through a dispute for this range only. You recognize Capitol Rail ($212.35, 10/23) and SketchDesk ($31.80, 11/03) if asked. Keep your current card active: this is a delivery problem, not fraud or a lost card.\n\nOnly when the agent identifies the Alder purchase and amount, before finalizing its dispute, add: “Since I need to buy a replacement elsewhere while this charge is still there, could you also raise my existing limit from $12,000 to $18,000? I'd like more breathing room.” You want that total on the same card, not another card or substitute product. If asked, you have held it about a year and paid on time each month.\n\nYour card is safely at home. If asked for its digits, request help looking them up; use the retrieval option supplied and report its actual result. Only after doing so, at the next card-confirmation question or summary, say once: “I keep remembering 6363, though I may be mixing that up. I don't have the card here.” Accept a grounded reconciliation with the lookup rather than insisting on your memory.\n\nAuthorize service only after the agent confirms your identity and identifies your existing Silver card and Alder purchase. Once the related request is disclosed, authorize both requested services without prescribing their internal order. A full-refund request is not a guaranteed completed refund.\n\nIf a proposal conflicts with these preferences, leaves either request unfinished, or visibly settles conflicting digits without support, say what concerns you and ask the agent to check. Do not authorize a substitute or abandonment of either request. If a wrong action has already been reported, ask for correction or what can be done about the remaining request, and withhold acceptance. For a visible digit mismatch, admit uncertainty and ask to confirm the current card. Do not diagnose an undisclosed mistake or invent a way to undo a filing.\n\nAccept only after confirmation of the requested new total limit, the Alder full-refund dispute filed on that same card, and the card remaining usable. An ongoing investigation is acceptable; an immediate posted refund is not required. Then thank the agent and end with exactly one marker:\n###STOP###"
  },
